{% endfor %}
## The {{ meta.file_name }} File

Put it in the repository root. The front matter fields `rating`, `spec` (a string), and `updated` (YYYY-MM-DD) are required. The body has a heading line with the rating spelled out, and a short plain-English "How AI Was Used" section. This is an example: replace the rating, the names in the heading line, the date, and the text with the project's own.

```markdown
---
rating: A2b
spec: "{{ meta.spec_version }}"
updated: 2026-10-05
---

# AI Code Rating

**ACR A2b** (Maintainer: Expert · AI Share: 26–50% · Oversight: Reviewed)

This project is rated with [AI Code Rating]({{ meta.site_url }}/spec/{{ meta.spec_version }}/), spec version {{ meta.spec_version }}.

## How AI Was Used

We use AI to write tests and some features, alongside code we write
ourselves. Every AI change goes through the same pull request review
as code written by people.
```

README badge, on its own line under the title:

```markdown
[![ACR A2b](https://img.shields.io/badge/ACR-A2b-{{ meta.badge_colour }})]({{ meta.file_name }})
```

